---
import Information from '../layouts/Information.astro';
import OperatorContact from '../components/OperatorContact.astro';
---

<Information
  title="Privacy information"
  description="How hosting, source links and optional external media affect your privacy."
>
  <p>
    This describes the current implementation. Operator identity and verified
    contact information must be completed before public launch.
  </p>
  <section aria-labelledby="hosting">
    <h2 id="hosting">Hosting and request information</h2>
    <p>
      The website is prepared for Cloudflare Workers hosting with static assets
      and a publication database. Visiting the website or reading its feed sends
      basic network information to the hosting provider, including your IP
      address, requested URL, request time and browser request headers.
      Cloudflare may process request and security logs to deliver and protect
      the service.
    </p>
    <p>
      The application has no visitor accounts, analytics, advertising or
      tracking pixels. Its publication database stores feed content, rather than
      visitor profiles. This does not mean that no information is collected by
      hosting or external providers.
    </p>
    <p>
      Retention of hosting logs depends on the provider and deployed
      configuration. No site-specific retention period is stated here until the
      operator has reviewed that configuration. See{' '}
      <a
        href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Cloudflare's privacy policy
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="links">
    <h2 id="links">Third-party source links</h2>
    <p>
      Opening an original source takes you to another website, which receives
      your network request and applies its own privacy practices. External links
      use referrer restrictions to avoid sending the referring page URL.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="media">
    <h2 id="media">External images and embeds</h2>
    <p>
      Third-party preview images and players load only after you choose LOAD
      CONTENT on that item. First-party images may load normally. Choosing OPEN
      ORIGINAL instead visits the source directly.
    </p>
    <p>
      Loading an image sends your IP address and browser request information to
      its image host, which may differ from the original publisher. Images are
      requested directly, without a proxy or rehosting.
    </p>
    <p>
      Optional YouTube, TikTok and Instagram players load in restricted frames.
      Reddit's official widget runs in a separate sandbox that cannot access the
      parent page's DOM. Loading these embeds sends requests to the provider and
      may cause additional requests to its service partners. The provider may
      receive request information, recognize an existing account, or use cookies
      and similar technologies, subject to your browser settings. No provider
      scripts or frames load before your action.
    </p>
    <p>
      The notice names the validated player provider or image hostname.
      Permission applies to that item on the current page; it is not saved
      between visits. Reloading the page requires another choice. Leaving media
      unloaded avoids those media requests.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="cookies">
    <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      The current application code does not set visitor cookies or store
      media-loading choices in local storage. Cloudflare security features, if
      enabled for a deployment, may use cookies. Loaded third-party content may
      set or read cookies or other browser storage. Browser settings can
      restrict these technologies, which may affect playback. See{' '}
      <a
        href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Cloudflare's cookie information
      </a>{' '}
      and each provider's policies.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="sharing">
    <h2 id="sharing">Sharing and privacy choices</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare processes information needed for hosting and security. Your
      browser sends information directly to external providers when you load
      media or open their links. Those providers may process information in
      other countries under their own policies. The application includes no
      third-party analytics or advertising integrations.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you email the operator, your address, message and attachments are
      processed to review and respond to the request, using the operator's email
      provider. Access and retention of complaint records must be reviewed
      before launch; no fixed retention period has been supplied.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="privacy-rights">
    <h2 id="privacy-rights">Your rights and questions</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on applicable law, you may have rights to request access,
      correction, deletion or restriction of personal information, object to
      processing, or complain to an appropriate data protection authority.
      Contact the operator about information they handle; requests about an
      external provider's independent processing should also be directed to that
      provider. The available rights depend on your circumstances and the
      applicable law.
    </p>
    <OperatorContact />
    <p>
      For content concerns, see <a href="/legal#removal">content removal</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Information>
